    {"eyebrow": "Why It's Different", "heading": "Landscaping Marketing Has to Follow the Seasons", "paragraphs": ["Landscaping companies don't have a steady flow of leads. You get buried in estimate requests in spring, slow down in midsummer, pick up again for fall cleanups and then wonder how to keep crews busy in winter. A marketing system for a landscaper has to work with that cycle, not against it.", "It also has to handle two very different kinds of customers: one-time design and install projects worth thousands, and recurring maintenance clients worth a steady monthly check. Both matter, and they're won in different ways."]},
    {
      "eyebrow": "Website",
      "heading": "A Landscaping Website That Shows Off Your Work",
